              "isInner": false,
              "settings": {
                "html": "<section class=\"sec-editorial bg-img-pricing text-center\">\n    <div class=\"overlay-layer overlay-warm-amber\"></div>\n    <div class=\"container\" style=\"max-width: 950px;\">\n      <div class=\"eyebrow-badge\">THE TURNING POINT</div>\n      <h2 class=\"sec-title\">So we asked a different question.</h2>\n      <p style=\"font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--ink-body); margin-bottom: 25px;\">\n        Not <em>\"how fast can AI spit out a book?\"</em> — everyone's racing to the bottom on that. We asked:\n      </p>\n      <div class=\"card-panel text-left\" style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid var(--amber-bright); font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.8;\">\n        <p style=\"font-style: italic; font-weight: 700; color: var(--blue-cobalt); margin-bottom: 15px;\">\n          \"What if one tool could research the niche, build a REAL book across any format, design the cover, AND format it to Amazon's exact spec — verified, correct, and compliant every single time?\"\n        </p>\n        <p style=\"font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--ink-body);\">\n          We encoded KDP's actual spec math into the engine. We built deterministic puzzle generators with mathematically-verified solutions. We tested files against Amazon's real Print Previewer until they passed with zero errors. The result is the tool we wish we'd had on day one.\n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>",
                "_element_id": "section-13-the-turning-point"
              },
              "elements": []
            }
          ]
        }
